          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The name حلیم (halīm) is spelled as Arabic ḥalīm, \"forbearing, patient\" (Lane, root ḥ-l-m), and reached Urdu through Persian, where ḥalīm also names a porridge of wheat and meat. A popular explanation is the dish's long, slow cooking, but how the dish came by the name is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
